 "extraction_notes": "Read from the HTML tables page with WebFetch; Table 5 read twice (row-wise and column-wise) and Table 6 read twice; all values agreed between reads. Six enamel samples x two gamma scenarios = 12 entries; '[scenario A]/[scenario B]' suffix is ours. Scenario A gamma = 658 +/- 160 uGy/a, scenario B = 342 +/- 63 uGy/a (Table 6 caption); these are back-derived from the bimodal summed age distribution, not measured, so recomputation should use them as given gamma inputs. Table 5 sediment U/Th/K (2.64 ppm, 2.80 ppm, 0.34 %) are 75% crust mean + 25% sediment mean and serve the beta dose rate only. In Table 5 the 'Removed enamel thickness' following the dentine block is mapped to removed_inner_um (dentine side) and the 'Removed thickness' in the sediment block to removed_outer_um. Enamel water 0% (stored as [0, null]). Table 5 footnote: removed thickness is an assumed value (20-60 um changes age by <1%); 10% error assumed on some inputs. Errors 1 sigma except apparent U-series ages (2 sigma, italics). Text: enamel 'ground and sieved <200 um'; inner and outer surfaces removed with a dentist drill. U-series by LA-MC-ICP-MS at RSES (Grun et al. 2014). Table 4 (13 sediment samples, ICP-MS) also available on the page; its K header reads 'ppm' but values (0.25-0.58) are evidently %.",
